## v0.6.8 – Private Alpha Deployment Preparation

**Date:** 2025-12-20 22:30 PST

### Changes Made:
- Migrated authentication from localStorage tokens to HttpOnly cookie-based auth
- Added CSRF protection with X-CSRF-Token header validation for state-changing requests
- Created CSRF middleware at backend/internal/middleware/csrf.go
- Updated auth middleware to read tokens from cookies first, fallback to Bearer header
- Enforced JWT_SECRET requirement in production (server fails fast if not set)
- Removed all localStorage token storage from frontend AuthContext
- Added `credentials: 'include'` to all frontend API calls for cookie transmission
- Created Invitation model for magic link invite system
- Added invitation token functions (create, validate, consume) in auth/tokens.go
- Created invitation handlers with admin-only routes for creating/managing invites
- Added public invitation validation endpoint GET /auth/invitation/:token
- Updated signup to accept optional invite_token parameter
- Invited users get auto-verified email (skip email verification flow)
- Added REQUIRE_INVITE env var for invite-only signup mode
- Created admin middleware for role-based access control
- Updated frontend signup page to handle ?invite=xxx query parameter
- Pre-fill and lock email field when signing up via invitation
- Created backend Dockerfile (multi-stage Alpine build)
- Created frontend Dockerfile (multi-stage with standalone output)
- Added output: 'standalone' to next.config.ts for Docker deployment
- Created docker-compose.yml for local testing with PostgreSQL
- Created .dockerignore files for both frontend and backend
- Fixed TypeScript errors from auth migration (accessToken -> isAuthenticated)
- Excluded test files from production TypeScript build

### Current Status:
- Backend builds and all existing tests pass
- Frontend builds successfully with standalone output
- Cookie-based auth fully implemented (replaces localStorage)
- Magic link invitation system complete (backend + frontend)
- Docker configuration ready for local testing and AWS deployment
- CSRF protection active for all POST/PATCH/DELETE requests

